{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1353815-touchstones-are-they-help-or-hindrance","id":1353815,"title":"Touchstones - are they help or hindrance?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-09T06:57:43-08:00","id":1353815,"title":"Touchstones - are they help or hindrance?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm preparing as ST for W:tF 2e chronicle, and I'm not sure how to use character Touchstones in play. The main question is probably - are touchstones helping with harmony stabilization (eg. character with harmony 7 is &quot;pulled&quot; towards spirit touchstone, either internally or externally), or are they forcing characters away from that sweet, sweet spot of harmony 5 (eg. character with harmony 7 is &quot;pulled&quot; towards flesh touchstone)?<br /> <br /> I personally lean towards the latter variant, mainly because I feel that harmony 5 should be pretty hard to achieve. But one of my players said that the former variant is the correct one, which means that Harmony 5 should be pretty hard to keep (when you have harmony 5, both touchstones are pulling you towards them).<br /> <br /> And there is really big chance that I missed something in Werewolf rulebook, so feel free to just point me to correct page/rules section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25828-aegnor","name":"Aegnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T08:38:43-08:00","id":1353854,"title":"","content":"The rules are pretty clear: as long as you're not at the heavy extreme of Harmony opposing a given Touchstone (so more than 3+ Harmony to retain use of your fleshly Touchstone, and less than 7 to retain use of your spiritual Touchstone), having a Touchstone adds dice to the roll to resist a breaking point away from that Touchstone's end of the meter. Having a Touchstone to the flesh makes progression towards the spirit less likely, and having a Touchstone to the spirit makes progression towards the flesh less likely. In both cases, they're modifying the breaking points you're already experiencing, not causing breaking points themselves (except when the Touchstone dies or is destroyed).<br /> <br /> Having a Touchstone isn't meant to make it harder to cultivate Harmony. Your anchoring relationships with both your fleshly and spiritual sides are good for you, not bad. As with all things Harmony, <i>losing balance</i> is bad: having only a flesh Touchstone will make you more prone to skewing above the balance point, and having only a spirit Touchstone will make you more prone to skewing below it. But having a Touchstone for both sides of your identity makes your Harmony less volatile, more stable: breaking points <i>in both directions</i> are less likely to shift your Harmony.<br /> <br /> With Touchstones, you're driving up and down hills. Without Touchstones, you're riding more of a rollercoaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}